 of a triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {40}^{∘}+m∠B+{95}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={180}^{∘}-{135}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $∠C$ is the largest angle, its opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ must be the longest side of the triangle. \n\nSince $∠A$ is the smallest angle, its opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ is the shortest side of the triangle.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nBC<AC<AB\n$$\n\nand therefore the required order is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BC},\\,\\overset{―}{AC},\\,\\overset{―}{AB}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "676e3d29-f6fa-5fe4-aae4-e9c0e974ee74" :knowledge-point/title "Ordering the Angles of a Triangle by Size Given the Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09cb2221-cd79-5d20-9c70-6c451fa4d6cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠B,\\,∠A,\\,∠C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487582} {:answer/id #uuid "33c9a741-c7b5-5a92-8afd-3b8939d1607e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠C,\\,∠B,\\,∠A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487666} {:answer/id #uuid "37046b81-4949-5cbe-8e48-ca60345a5ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠C,\\,∠A,\\,∠B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487672} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4967cd-d07f-5f8f-b17c-148202bda167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠B,\\,∠C,\\,∠A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487860} {:answer/id #uuid "b730feb5-55fe-5332-bb20-b247934c7532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠A,\\,∠B,\\,∠C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d4967cd-d07f-5f8f-b17c-148202bda167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answe